<title>GERMANY: Henkel acquires Diversified Technology.</title>
<headline>Henkel acquires Diversified Technology.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany</dateline>
<text>
<p>German consumer products and chemicals group Henkel KGaA said Tuesday it had acquired Diversified Technology Inc., weeks after announcing a major takeover in the United States.</p>
<p>Henkel, fresh from acquiring U.S. adhesives maker Loctite Corp. late last year, said Diversified Technology, a maker of lubricants used in the aluminium and steel industries, would help expand the German group's international metal chemicals business.</p>
<p>Diversified Technology most recently posted sales of $12 million and employs 30, Henkel said. Terms of the Diversified Technology acquisition were not disclosed.</p>
</text>
